// # sec/cap/zig — Zig rewrite of the cap-system
//
// Logline: Phase 4 of the 2026-09-11 memory-safety plan. The leaf
//          integer comparison that powers every oo_cap_require_*
//          gate is implemented in Zig (cap_check.zig) with bounds-
//          checked arithmetic. C ABI export (oo_cap_check_bits_zig)
//          keeps the rest of oodar in C. Future commits will
//          incrementally migrate more cap-system files.
//
// Setup:  Build with `zig build` from this directory (yields
//         liboodar_cap_check.a static lib). Tests with `zig build
//         test`. The umbrella TU does NOT yet link against this lib;
//         a future commit will add the link rule + a C-side call to
//         oo_cap_check_bits_zig from one of the existing gates.
//
// Beats:
//   1. cap_check.zig — oo_cap_check_bits_zig(i64, i64) -> i32.
//   2. cap_check_test.zig — 5 unit tests (zero / match / mismatch /
//      negative / i64 extremes).
//   3. build.zig — static lib + test step.
